      "id": "PR_kwDOOqAYW87m5Nyy",
      "title": "Field Descriptors and repeatable CoAP options",
      "url": "https://github.com/ietf-wg-schc/draft-ietf-schc-8824-update/pull/2",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "marco-tiloca-sics",
      "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "This PR addresses two narrowly scoped points:\r\n\r\n* Section 5.1 - A single Field Descriptor can pertain to multiple adjacent instances of the same CoAP option that are treated as grouped together (e.g., see Section 5.4).\r\n\r\n* Section 5.4.1 - Handling a variable number of path segments and query parameters requires different SCHC Rules to cover the different possibilities. (E.g., a Uri-Path Option that is present and has no option value is **not** equivalent to an absent Uri-Path Option)\r\n\r\nEDIT: More details at https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/schc/uQ9E77-g0dsHsjbXWI63yaV8tdg/",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-16T07:36:39Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-06-16T07:45:50Z",
